.TH GETDENTS 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
getdents \- read legacy Linux directory records
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <sys/getdents.h>
.B ssize_t getdents(unsigned int descriptor, struct linux_dirent* buffer,
.B                  unsigned int byte_count);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reads raw Linux x86\-64 legacy directory records.  Advance by d_reclen; the
NUL-terminated d_name is variable length and d_type is the last byte of each
record.  The name array declaration represents only its first byte.  Prefer
getdents64 and dirent64_next for new code.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns bytes read, zero at end of directory, or \-1 with errno set.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR getdents64 (3crunch),
.BR dirent64_next (3crunch),
.BR getdents (2)
